        "delta": "Production has staged changes, and nothing has been deployed there. I haven't deployed anything.\n\n**Production hasn't been deployed yet.** Every service and the volume is a first-time create, so the next deploy would introduce the whole environment. The diff has 9 changes in total. These are the ones it listed:\n\n- **`web` (create):**\n  - `managedHostnames`: a `www` hostname pointing at port 80\n  - `env.API_URL` = `https://api.production.acme.test`\n  - `env.LOG_LEVEL` = `info`\n  - `env.SESSION_KEY` = a secret value, which I can't see\n- **`db` (create):** it mounts the `pgdata` volume at `/var/lib/postgresql/data`.\n- **`worker` (create):** no settings are staged for it.\n- **`pgdata` volume (create):** Docker storage, not yet deployed.\n\nThis looks like the full initial setup for production, not a single tweak. It doesn't look like the `LOG_LEVEL` change you shipped to staging. Production's `LOG_LEVEL` is `info`, and staging's is now `warn`.\n\nDo you want me to deploy this to production? If you'd rather change something first, such as `LOG_LEVEL`, tell me and I'll stage it. I won't deploy until you say so.",
